{"id": "sc900_p3_q071", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "security_compliance_identity", "objective": "security_compliance_concepts", "subobjective": "encryption and hashing", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A team needs to verify that a downloaded file has not been changed, but it does not need to recover the original file contents from that check value. Which operation is designed for that integrity check?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Authorization"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Federation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Hashing"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Role assignment"}], "correct_answer": "c", "explanation": "Hashing produces a one-way value that can be used to check integrity. It is not intended as a reversible way to recover the original content, which is the job of encryption and decryption.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"], "tags": ["encryption and hashing", "encryption_and_hashing"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "encryption_and_hashing", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-concepts-methodologies/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-security_compliance_concepts", "semantic_family_id": "hashing_integrity", "stem_style": "distinction_comparison", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q072", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_identity_types_and_function", "subobjective": "types of identities, including agent ID", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A partner user from another organization needs access to a company's Microsoft 365 resources without becoming an employee account in that company's on-premises directory. Which identity type is designed for that scenario?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "An Azure DDoS Protection policy"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A network security group"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A retention label"}, {"id": "d", "text": "An external or guest identity in Microsoft Entra ID"}], "correct_answer": "d", "explanation": "Microsoft Entra ID supports external/guest identities so partners can be authenticated and authorized without being created as internal employee accounts in the company's on-premises directory.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"], "tags": ["types of identities, including agent ID", "identity_types_including_agent_id"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "identity_types_including_agent_id", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-basic-services-identity-types/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_identity_types_and_function", "semantic_family_id": "entra_guest_identity", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q073", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_access_management", "subobjective": "Microsoft Entra roles and RBAC", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "What does assigning a Microsoft Entra role to a user, group, or workload identity actually control?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "The Microsoft Entra management permissions that identity has in the tenant"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The DDoS mitigation threshold for a public IP"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The retention period of a SharePoint site"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The SKU of Azure Firewall"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Microsoft Entra roles are an RBAC mechanism that grants permissions to manage Entra and related directory resources. They do not set DDoS thresholds, retention periods, or firewall SKUs.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"], "tags": ["Microsoft Entra roles and RBAC", "entra_roles_rbac"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "entra_roles_rbac", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-access-management-capabilities/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_access_management", "semantic_family_id": "entra_roles_rbac", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q074", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_entra", "objective": "entra_authentication", "subobjective": "password protection and management", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Which Microsoft Entra password-management capability lets a user reset a forgotten password without calling the help desk, after completing required verification?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Azure Bastion"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Self-service password reset"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Defender Threat Intelligence"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Content explorer"}], "correct_answer": "b", "explanation": "Self-service password reset is the Entra password-management capability that lets users reset passwords after proving their identity. Bastion, Defender TI, and Content explorer are not password-reset tools.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"], "tags": ["password protection and management", "password_protection_management"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "password_protection_management", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-authentication-capabilities/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-entra_authentication", "semantic_family_id": "sspr_password_management", "stem_style": "capability_selection", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q075", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "azure_infrastructure_security", "subobjective": "network segmentation with Azure virtual networks", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Why can resources in the same Azure virtual network communicate privately without using the public internet by default?", "choices": [{"id": "b", "text": "Because every virtual network issues FIDO2 credentials"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Because virtual networks classify Microsoft 365 documents"}, {"id": "a", "text": "Because a virtual network provides a private network boundary for those resources"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Because virtual networks replace Microsoft Entra ID"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "An Azure virtual network is a private network boundary. Resources inside it can communicate using private networking rather than being exposed across the public internet by default.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"], "tags": ["network segmentation with Azure virtual networks", "azure_virtual_network_segmentation"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "azure_virtual_network_segmentation", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-basic-security-capabilities-azure/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-azure_infrastructure_security", "semantic_family_id": "vnet_private_boundary", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q076", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "defender_xdr", "subobjective": "Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A cloud-app security team wants alerts when a user downloads an unusually large amount of data from a sanctioned SaaS application. Which Microsoft Defender service is designed to monitor that cloud-app activity?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Microsoft Purview Records Management"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Azure Key Vault"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Entra Domain Services"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps"}], "correct_answer": "d", "explanation": "Defender for Cloud Apps monitors cloud-application activity and can alert on unusual behavior such as abnormal downloads. Records management, Key Vault, and Entra Domain Services do not provide that cloud-app anomaly monitoring.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"], "tags": ["Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps", "defender_for_cloud_apps"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "defender_for_cloud_apps", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-threat-protection-with-microsoft-365-defender/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-defender_xdr", "semantic_family_id": "defender_for_cloud_apps_anomaly", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q077", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "azure_security_management", "subobjective": "cloud workload protection", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Which example is a cloud workload protection outcome rather than a posture-recommendation outcome?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Detecting malware or suspicious behavior on a running virtual machine or container"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Listing a missing encryption setting on a storage account"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Reporting that a resource does not meet a policy baseline"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Suggesting that diagnostic logs should be enabled"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Cloud workload protection is concerned with threats against running workloads, such as malware or suspicious runtime behavior. Missing encryption, policy gaps, and logging recommendations are posture-management findings.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"], "tags": ["cloud workload protection", "cloud_workload_protection"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "cloud_workload_protection", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-management-capabilities-of-azure/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-azure_security_management", "semantic_family_id": "cloud_workload_protection", "stem_style": "distinction_comparison", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q078", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_security_solutions", "objective": "microsoft_sentinel", "subobjective": "threat detection and mitigation in Microsoft Sentinel", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "After Microsoft Sentinel creates an incident, which capability helps analysts examine related alerts, entities, and evidence in one investigation view?", "choices": [{"id": "b", "text": "Azure DDoS Protection SKU selection"}, {"id": "a", "text": "Incident investigation in Microsoft Sentinel"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sensitivity label visual marking"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Temporary Access Pass lifetime settings"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Microsoft Sentinel incidents group related alerts and support investigation of entities and evidence. DDoS SKUs, label marking, and TAP lifetime are not Sentinel investigation capabilities.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"], "tags": ["threat detection and mitigation in Microsoft Sentinel", "sentinel_threat_detection_mitigation"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "sentinel_threat_detection_mitigation", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-security-capabilities-of-azure-sentinel/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-microsoft_sentinel", "semantic_family_id": "sentinel_incident_investigation", "stem_style": "capability_selection", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q079", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_compliance_solutions", "objective": "purview_insider_risk_ediscovery_audit", "subobjective": "audit", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "A compliance investigator needs to answer who performed a specific admin action in Microsoft 365 and when it occurred. Which Microsoft Purview solution is designed for that activity-log search?", "choices": [{"id": "a", "text": "Azure Web Application Firewall"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Microsoft Entra Verified ID"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Microsoft Purview Audit"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Azure Bastion"}], "correct_answer": "c", "explanation": "Microsoft Purview Audit provides searchable records of user and administrator activities in supported Microsoft services. WAF, Verified ID, and Bastion do not provide that Microsoft 365 activity-log search.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "tags": ["audit", "audit"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "audit", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-purview-risk-compliance-governance/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-purview_insider_risk_ediscovery_audit", "semantic_family_id": "audit", "stem_style": "short_scenario", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
{"id": "sc900_p3_q080", "exam": "SC-900", "domain": "microsoft_compliance_solutions", "objective": "service_trust_privacy", "subobjective": "privacy principles of Microsoft", "difficulty": "beginner", "type": "multiple_choice", "stem": "Which Microsoft privacy principle is most directly reflected when customers can decide how their data is collected and used?", "choices": [{"id": "b", "text": "Network segmentation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Privileged Identity Management"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Records declaration"}, {"id": "a", "text": "Customer control over their data"}], "correct_answer": "a", "explanation": "Microsoft's privacy principles include customer control: customers should be able to control their data. Segmentation, PIM, and records declaration are other security or compliance capabilities, not that privacy principle.", "references": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"], "tags": ["privacy principles of Microsoft", "microsoft_privacy_principles"], "source": {"title": "Microsoft Learn", "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"}, "metadata": {"origin": "manual", "batch": "phase3-batch-08", "blueprint_leaf_id": "microsoft_privacy_principles", "source_authority": "microsoft_learn", "source_urls": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/describe-compliance-management-capabilities-microsoft/"], "source_retrieved_at": "2026-09-11", "source_family_id": "learn-service_trust_privacy", "semantic_family_id": "microsoft_privacy_control", "stem_style": "direct_concept", "future_probe_suitability": "eligible", "authoring_origin": "original_from_official_source"}}
